{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3048","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3048","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3048\",\"parent_revision\":\"a1823dabdae5c52e57b68569261458f2860d138dfcb554b42472f37ee4d3181c\",\"root_revision\":\"a1823dabdae5c52e57b68569261458f2860d138dfcb554b42472f37ee4d3181c\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nDiscovered while fixing #2978's residual gap (unregistered legacy-`.md` headings not getting the `unknown__` prefix): the existing Hypothesis property test `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_github_sync.py::TestSectionRoundTripProperty::test_write_render_parse_round_trip_is_lossless` fails when Hypothesis shrinks to a `section_name` containing punctuation \u2014 the minimal failing example found was `section_name=':PRIORITY'`.\\n\\nConfirmed via `git stash` that this failure is **pre-existing on `main`**, independent of any change made while fixing #2978/#2969 \u2014 it is not a regression introduced by either of those fixes.\\n\\nThis is the same *class* of defect as #2968 (heading_to_unknown_key's non-alphanumeric-collapsing encoding produces duplicate/lossy keys), but #2968's confirmed reproduction is specifically about **underscore vs. space** collisions. This failure is triggered by **punctuation** (`:`) and manifests as a duplicate-key bug across the full `render_issue_body` \u2192 `parse_issue_body` \u2192 `merge_item` round trip, not just a key-collision at the `heading_to_unknown_key` level \u2014 worth scoping separately from #2968 rather than assuming the same fix covers both, though the two are almost certainly related (same underlying non-injective encoding in `backlog_core/rendering.py`) and may end up resolved by the same design decision.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Root cause confirmed: identify exactly which step (render, parse, or merge) introduces the duplicate key or data loss for a punctuation-containing section name\\n- [ ] Relationship to #2968 clarified: same root cause (fix together) or genuinely distinct mechanism (fix separately) \u2014 state which and why\\n- [ ] `test_write_render_parse_round_trip_is_lossless` passes for the full space of section names Hypothesis can generate, including punctuation\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the backlog system**, I want **section names containing punctuation to round-trip losslessly through render/parse/merge** so that **grooming content isn't silently duplicated or corrupted for any section name outside the plain-alphanumeric-with-spaces case**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Discovered during #2978 residual-gap fix investigation, 2026-08-20 \u2014 session continuing #2956/#2970/#2974/#2969 backlog-integrity work\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Related**: #2968 (same encoding function, different collision trigger \u2014 space/underscore vs. punctuation)\\n- **Reproduction**: `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_github_sync.py::TestSectionRoundTripProperty::test_write_render_parse_round_trip_is_lossless -x` on current `main` (confirmed failing independent of any in-flight PR via `git stash`)\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"4ec3ae7c0b5e6156e393e05140ce53eb0bc8c53e170afacb958c7787b6fcfbd2\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPuiA_w\"}"}